#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'HELP'
Pi workspace quick reference
============================

Start from no tmux sessions:
  pi-start                 Start tmux, ensure pi-personal, and attach to it.
  pi-start --mobile        Start full-width conversation windows.
  pi-start secretary       Start/open the tmux secretary grid and attach to it.
  pi-secretary --herdr     Open the separate Herdr secretary surface.
  pi-start project [DIR]   Open a project workspace (DIR defaults to $PWD).
  pi-start host            Open pi-personal and select its explicit pi-host pane.
  pi-start all              Start pi-personal and the secretary grid.
  pi-restart                Kill all tmux sessions, then run pi-start all.
  pi-restart --mobile       Rebuild each Pi conversation as its own full-width window.

Help and restart:
  pi --help-custom           Show this guide from any shell.
  pi-start help              Show this guide through the managed launcher.
  pi-restart                 Kill all tmux sessions and boot pi-start all.

Run Pi directly:
  cd REPOSITORY && pi       Normal policy-controlled durable root session.
  pi-host                   Explicit unsandboxed host-maintenance session.
  pi-root-session migrate --dry-run
                            Inspect legacy root-session migration.
  pi-root-session migrate  Copy selected histories into stable roots.
  pi-root-session cleanup --repository PATH
                            Review stale worktrees before explicit cleanup.

In Pi:
  /goal <objective>          Continue the same goal until completion or a bound.
  /goal status|pause|resume  Inspect or control the active goal.
  /goal clear                Remove the active goal.
  /goal --tokens 100k ...    Add a provider-token budget to a goal.
  Enter while busy           Steer the current run (after the current tool batch).
  Alt-Enter while busy       Queue a follow-up after the run settles.
  /fast on|off|status        Toggle OpenAI priority service tier.
  /subagents-doctor          Inspect subagent discovery and runtime routing.
  Ctrl-g                     Browse conversation history without losing the prompt.

Project tmux workspaces:
  cd REPOSITORY && pidev    Neovim on the left, Pi on the right.
  cd REPOSITORY && pidev --mobile
                            Pi gets a full-width window; no Neovim split is created.
  pidev --help              Show the managed project-launcher help.

Tmux sessions and switching:
  Ctrl-a p                  Switch to pi-personal.
  Ctrl-a g                  Switch to pisec (if it is running).
  Ctrl-a \                  Toggle the previous tmux session.
  tmux ls                   List sessions.
  tmux attach -t NAME      Attach to a named session.

Secretary projects:
  pi-secretary --herdr      Open one Herdr Space per registered project; optional backend, does not replace pisec.
  pisec                     Open the default projects without restarting live panes.
  pisec --mobile            Put each active secretary conversation in its own full-width window.
  pisec activate ALIAS ... Replace the active project set.
  pisec swap OLD NEW       Replace one active project without changing order.
  pisec list                Print the registered project records.
  pi-secretary-stats        Summarize secretary session/run time and token usage.
  /subagents-fleet          Explicitly inspect private child runs.

Herdr navigation:
  Ctrl-b w                  Open the Spaces/workspace picker.
  Ctrl-b h/j/k/l            Move between panes; Ctrl-b c, n, p navigate tabs.
  Ctrl-b b                  Toggle the sidebar; Ctrl-b q detaches.
  Ctrl-b ?                  Show Herdr help; Ctrl-b Ctrl-b sends a literal prefix to Pi.
  Space/workspace           Project/context container; tab is a layout; pane is a terminal; agent is its process.
  Agents view               Selects an exact process; a one-secretary Space has no useful current-Space filter until workers are added.
  kitty --version           Diagnose the known Kitty 0.31/0.32 Backspace press/release bug; upgrade Kitty >= 0.48.1.

Recovery:
  pi-restart                Replace every tmux workspace with a fresh Pi grid.
  pi-start personal         Recreate missing personal panes and attach there.
  pi-start --mobile all     Boot personal and secretary in full-width mobile windows.
  pi-personal --ensure      Repair personal two-pane windows without switching clients.
  pi-personal --mobile --ensure
                            Repair personal full-width windows without switching clients.
  pisec launch              Repair/rebuild the secretary grid when panes are idle.

The ordinary pi launcher owns workspace selection and sandbox policy. Do not
pass sandbox/trust flags to it; use pi-host only when unsandboxed host access is
intentional.
HELP
